🐧 Day 14 — Linux Boot Process & System Startup

📌 What I Learned

Today I learned how a Linux system starts from Power ON and reaches the Login Screen / Terminal.

🔄 Linux Boot Process

Power ON
   ↓
BIOS / UEFI
   ↓
Bootloader (GRUB)
   ↓
Linux Kernel
   ↓
systemd (PID 1)
   ↓
Services Start
   ↓
Login Screen / Terminal

💻 Topics Covered

- ⚡ Power ON and hardware initialization
- 🖥️ BIOS / UEFI
- 🚀 GRUB Bootloader
- 🐧 Linux Kernel
- ⚙️ systemd and PID 1
- 🔧 Service initialization
- 🖥️ Login Screen / Terminal

🧠 Key Learning

The Linux boot process happens in multiple stages, and each stage has a specific responsibility.

Understanding this flow is important for troubleshooting:

- Boot failures
- Kernel loading issues
- Service startup problems
- System initialization issues

